From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypt32: streamed CryptMsgOpenToDecode hands the content to the stream output (3758)

CryptMsgUpdate on a message opened with CMSG_STREAM_INFO for decoding only
collected the bytes: the stream output was never called. The inner content of
data and signed messages (and the decrypted content of enveloped ones) is now
handed to the callback as it arrives, ending with a final call; a header that
is not a message fails with CRYPT_E_ASN1_BADTAG as soon as it arrives, a final
update with the content incomplete with CRYPT_E_STREAM_INSUFFICIENT_DATA, and
before a streamed message ends CryptMsgGetParam says CRYPT_E_STREAM_MSG_NOT_READY
(CMSG_ENVELOPE_ALGORITHM_PARAM and the recipients of an enveloped message are
there as soon as its header is). CMSG_CTRL_DECRYPT on a streamed enveloped
message starts the decryption of what has arrived and what follows. The five
todo_wine lines of test_decode_msg_update pass. CORE review: security
(patches/notes/3758.txt).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XZFS4SPPzeH5d2c1MuzqCS

Rebased at integration (integ-2026-10) onto 5622 (stubs-6d): CDecodeMsg_DecodeEnvelopedContent keeps 5622's rebuilt-DER handling and 3758's early-header release.
